## 6. Real-Time Hardware Latency & Pipeline Constraints

To run on an FPGA control system without causing qubit decoherence, Aether's timing parameters must satisfy:

$$t_{\text{decode}} = t_{\text{ingest}} + t_{\text{UF\_growth}} + t_{\text{peeling}} \le \frac{\tau_{\text{coherence}}}{N_{\text{rounds}}}$$

| Subsystem Parameter | Symbol | Target Threshold Bound |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Physical Qubit Coherence Time** | $\tau_{\text{coherence}}$ | $\sim 100 \; \mu\text{s}$ (Superconducting) |
| **Syndrome Round Window** | $T_{\text{round}}$ | $200 \text{ ns} - 1 \; \mu\text{s}$ |
| **Growth Phase Cycles** | $N_{\text{growth}}$ | $\le \frac{d}{2}$ rounds ($d = \text{code distance}$) |
| **Peeling Execution Complexity** | $T_{\text{peeling}}$ | $O(\vert{}E_{\text{solid}}\vert{}) \approx O(d^3)$ linear steps |
| **Clock Frequency (FPGA Logic)** | $f_{\text{clk}}$ | $250 \text{ MHz} - 500 \text{ MHz}$ ($2 - 4 \text{ ns per cycle}$) |

